Yeah. So the action scene is the typical side scroller that we're all familiar with, um, where there's

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:57.480
platforming and very easy battles, at least in the beginning, uh, where you just hit them

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.940
with some kind of projectile or a yo-yo.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:07.820
Um, and then there are these doors scattered around, um, that you go into and that puts you into that

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:17.700
first person sort of isometric view, not isometric, first person view of a room that has doors or not doors on all of the walls.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:21.830
They're all pretty much as square rooms and you have interaction options.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:33.310
Like you can choose to use a hammer that you found and knock on the walls and see if there's anything hidden or just interacting with characters that you may come across.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:37.770
It's very, uh, like Ultima, like from back in the day.

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.010
Ultima is a great example.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:42.170
Yeah. And I just kind of want to, let's just break that down even a little further.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:48.070
Right. So you, so you're given the options of go hit take and your tools, right?

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:53.930
Yeah. So, so with go, you choose which direction you want to go in, which includes leaving the room.

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:59.430
Yeah. That might not be like a parent who don't realize that it's first person.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:05.750
You know, I don't know if necessarily as a kid, I would have understood right away that, oh, this is from my eyeballs.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.110
You know, like I would have probably still been looking for me in the room.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:21.690
Well, they also have a little tool in the bottom left corner that has a, another version of Mikey that sort of puts him in that space, uh, in a weird, uh, amorphous way.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:23.810
Yeah. Facing the direction that you'll be advancing.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:25.550
Yeah. Yep. So they have that.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:33.730
Then there's hit, which to me at first seemed like, okay, so like, I guess when I see things in the room, I'll use my hammer, which is something you get immediately.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.630
Yeah. I'll use my hammer and just hit things.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:39.210
It never occurred to me like, oh, I should be hitting on the walls.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:43.550
Right. Yeah. You should just honestly be hitting and using your hammer everywhere in the room.

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:45.890
Spot the pixel. Just, just, just decide.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:47.850
Well, it's really which wall though, right?

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:49.450
Like. I don't actually know.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:56.470
I think that. I don't think that you can like hit the lower part of one wall and be wrong and then hit the higher part of the same wall.

00:15:56.610 --> 00:16:01.770
I remember, I remember, uh, looking at a video to try and get farther because I couldn't figure it out.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:07.290
And I had already hit a wall that was supposed to open into a door.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:16.310
I will say that if I tried the dead centers, I was using a guide, but if I tried like the dead centers, it seemed to be working, but I never really tried like the left, right.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:21.470
Yeah. You know? So maybe it is like, you know, you just have to be perfectly centered on each wall to tap.

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:26.130
And hit usually is, it doesn't really do what you expected to do.

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:28.210
Most of them hit lets you find things.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:29.630
Like that's what I know.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:35.350
It's like hit, you hit the wall and like a key will appear or you hit the wall and like something falls out of the wall or something.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:40.370
And then, then the hammer lets you like uncover something, like break the wall down and there's like a door or something.

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:45.110
Right. Yeah. And to Joe, to Joe's point, I think like, that's the opposite of what I would expect hit to do.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:51.070
I would think hit is more of a combat thing where like, Oh, I've seen somebody else in the room, like that Eskimo guy.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:53.030
And you're like, okay, is he bad?

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:53.970
Like, do I hit him?

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:55.530
Does he have any point?

00:16:55.890 --> 00:17:03.490
No, he, um, there, there's a really bad translation error with him where, where he, he essentially just says, there's nothing here.

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:10.630
Yeah. There's nothing here, but it was actually, you know, in the Japanese version, I'm not, I don't have the perfect translation with me, but it was more of like a joke of like,

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:11.930
how did I get here?

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:16.950
You know, like that's kind of funny in context, instead of just saying, there is nothing here.

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.250
Cause he says like, doesn't he say I am Eskimo.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.410
There's nothing here. Yeah.

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:21.630
That's exactly what he says.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:25.730
It's, it's, it's, oh, it's very close to, I am error, you know, like from Legend of Zelda 2.

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.650
Yeah. Which we haven't gotten to yet.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.230
So don't feel bad. I don't know that reference.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:38.110
Okay. And then you have take, which is obvious, grab whatever you want and tools where you get to go through all of your different tools.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:46.170
However, sometimes you need specific tools to do specific things in rooms and it's not abundantly clear which tool you need.

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:49.450
So that just also becomes a game of like, let me try each tool.

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:52.030
Yeah. See what happens, you know, like maybe the candle works here.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:59.790
Right. And to that point too, there are just a bunch of things that, things like that where you, you would never know to do this.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:01.590
I think I found this on online.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:09.230
There's someone that you, you hit, you hit them and they say, they say something, some terribly mistranslated.

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:10.670
Like what are you doing or something?

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.450
Yeah. And they'll be like, well, why are you doing this?

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:17.330
But you hit this person five times and on the fifth time they give you the candle.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.550
The candle. That's right.

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:19.650
Yeah. It's ridiculous.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:24.650
And that's the, that's the most well-known example of that in this game of just very frustrating.

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:29.490
I'll tell you what's funny is, is that there's a guy who goes by the name of the Mexican runner.

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.310
