00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:42.090
He is the, he is a guy who completed every single NES game that was released, uh, under clear definitions of like what it means to like complete that game.

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:44.710
His run for Goonies two.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:47.790
And he tries not to use guides when necessary.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:50.050
His run for Goonies two was seven hours long.

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:53.930
Wow. Mostly him just going through trying to figure out what am I doing?

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:57.390
Cause he didn't have a guide and didn't know how to figure things out.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:19:04.310
The chat was trying to help him out a little and it just became like this crazy thing where it's like, there's a guy who was really good at NES games.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:05.790
He's beat every single one of them.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.730
And it took him seven hours to figure out Goonies two.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:19.450
Like there are some hints in the game that like if you, when you get the transceiver where you can talk to some of your, because you're trying to rescue the Goonies, uh, when you, and you were trying to talk to them.

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:23.670
I, there's one where you're talking to whatever the blonde girl's name is.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:27.790
Uh, but she says, I'm freezing in here.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:30.410
And it's like, Oh, I gotta go to that like cold world.

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:39.510
And I'll probably find her in one of those doors, but nothing in the game at all says that you should abuse an old man or whoever that is.

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:42.730
Uh, and just keep hitting them until they, you drop it.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.950
And especially because you need to do it five times.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.870
Yeah. You're well past the point where you're like, okay, nothing happens.

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:51.290
That's yeah. That's the problem is that that, that first clue is actually okay.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:54.170
In my book, like it's a little vague, but I'll take it.

00:19:54.690 --> 00:20:03.110
The, the hit, if it, if it's going to give you anything, it should at least hint towards the fact of like, ow, that almost hurt, you know?

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.810
And then like change it each time.

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:07.990
You know, like, I don't understand why you had somebody to get a candle in the first place.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:10.130
Why they couldn't just figure out like, Oh, let's hide this in a wall.

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:11.670
The Goonies have changed. Yeah.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:20.790
The only thing that I could think of that's trying to, to, to beckon you to do that is that the person that greets you isn't like really nice to you.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.370
They say, go away.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.550
Okay. So I guess you're supposed to assault them then.

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:26.610
Yeah. That's what you do to anybody who says go away.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.510
Just let them know your stance on things.

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:29.890
Right. And then they'll give you a candle.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:39.250
I will mention that in the, the last thing from the manual that I have is that in the game hint section, which is the final page, it does say very, very first thing.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:50.750
It says, if you get stuck in a dead end room, try tapping the center of the room with a hammer or hand mark, possibly use the hand mark and tap the ceiling, the front wall or the floor.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:54.610
If you try this with the hammer, you may be able to open up a secret passage.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:55.610
Who knows?

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:57.110
Now, who knows?

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.170
You know, I, I liked that.

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:00.430
I think that they also tried to pretend like, you know, like they don't know.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:01.450
That's just a vague thing.

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:05.910
Yeah. Like maybe try it where it's actually like very important to the game.

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:11.350
But it also seems kind of weird that this is the first mention you're getting of it is in the hint section of the game.

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:13.310
It's never brought up in the game.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.070
And it just seems like a huge flaw.

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:22.190
So I think what I'm getting at is it's nice that this action scene or no, this is the adventure scene, right?

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:25.130
Mm hmm. Yeah. It's nice that the adventure scene exists.

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:27.210
It's really poorly executed on.

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:50.470
I think that I don't know how much of this can be blamed on poor communication in the game, because I think that a lot of the more abstract game concepts that we've come across so far in the NES chronological exploration so far have been things that they had to explain the manual.

00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:53.030
Like you had to get to the manual to understand them.

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:55.150
Do you know what I'm getting at?

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:56.530
No, I totally agree. I agree with that.

00:21:56.530 --> 00:22:05.110
I guess what I'm saying is now that we've talked about the go hit, take tools, like all these different things, slapping a person five times, like all those things.

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:11.770
In hindsight, this adventure scene is a cool idea of like exploring rooms in the first person and being able to actually like tap on the wall.

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:13.970
I do agree. But it doesn't work at the end of the day.

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:15.990
Right. At the end of the day, this is the game's flaw.

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:23.590
And the action scene, while not being more interesting than the adventure scene, at least that's like that works.

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:25.750
Right. You know. And they got that cool song.

