00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:08.890
We're from the future.

00:23:10.310 --> 00:23:18.470
And we all, I mean, I also get what went in with the expectation that this is going to be way too hidden for my taste.

00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:22.030
Yeah, just because of the archaic systems that it set up for you.

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:24.030
And I guess that's going to bring me to my next question.

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:27.450
Was the first person approach the right thing to do here?

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:35.530
Not in hindsight, just saying like at the time, is that like a, is that a neat enough selling point to say like, screw all the fundamental flaws with this.

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:42.170
Let's let's ship this product with this first person exploration thing because it's a neat new thing for the NES.

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:48.150
I don't think that the actual first person mechanics are the flaw.

00:23:48.350 --> 00:23:49.890
I think it's just the level design.

00:23:50.150 --> 00:23:51.650
Yeah, I don't think it helps or hurts.

00:23:51.770 --> 00:23:53.770
I think it's just first person, whatever.

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:56.770
Fine. But yeah, it's, it's the, it's the way that everything's implemented.

00:23:56.950 --> 00:24:00.010
